+# Stripe Payment Integration Example
+
+This document shows how to integrate Stripe payments with your existing order system.
+
+## Example: Complete Payment Flow
+
+### 1. Create an Order and Initiate Payment
+
+```kotlin
+@Service
+class CheckoutService(
+  private val orderService: OrderService,
+  private val stripePaymentService: StripePaymentService,
+  private val propertyService: PropertyService
+) {
+  
+  suspend fun initiateCheckout(
+    userId: UUID,
+    productId: UUID,
+    stripeProductId: String,
+    stripePriceId: String
+  ): PaymentSession {
+    // Create order in your system
+    val order = orderService.create(
+      OrderCreateInput(
+        productId = productId.toString(),
+        user = UserConnectOrCreate(connect = UserWhereUniqueInput(id = userId.toString())),
+        invoiceRecipientEmail = "customer@example.com",
+        invoiceRecipientName = "Customer Name",
+        paymentMethod = PaymentMethodDto.CreditCard,
+        callbackUrl = "${propertyService.appHost}/payment/${order.id}/callback",
+        targetGroup = ProductTargetGroup.individual
+      )
+    )
+    
+    // Create Stripe payment session
+    val session = stripePaymentService.createPaymentSessionForOrder(
+      order = order,
+      stripeProductId = stripeProductId,
+      stripePriceId = stripePriceId,
+      successUrl = "${propertyService.appHost}/payment/${order.id}/success",
+      cancelUrl = "${propertyService.appHost}/payment/${order.id}/cancel"
+    )
+    
+    // Redirect user to session.checkoutUrl
+    return session
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### 2. Handle Webhook (Automatic)
+
+The `StripeWebhookController` automatically handles webhooks at `/api/stripe/webhook`.
+
+When a payment succeeds:
+1. Stripe sends webhook to your endpoint
+2. Webhook is verified using signature
+3. `OrderService.handlePaymentCallback()` is called
+4. Order is marked as paid
+5. License is created (if applicable)
+
+### 3. Handle User Return After Payment
+
+```kotlin
+@Controller
+class PaymentReturnController(
+  private val orderService: OrderService
+) {
+  
+  @GetMapping("/payment/{orderId}/success")
+  suspend fun paymentSuccess(
+    @PathVariable orderId: String
+  ): ResponseEntity<String> {
+    // Note: Always verify payment status via webhook, not just the return URL
+    // The webhook is the source of truth
+    
+    val order = orderService.findById(UUID.fromString(orderId))
+    
+    return if (order.isPaid) {
+      ResponseEntity.ok("""
+        <html>
+          <body>
+            <h1>Payment Successful!</h1>
+            <p>Thank you for your purchase.</p>
+            <p>Order ID: ${order.id}</p>
+          </body>
+        </html>
+      """.trimIndent())
+    } else {
+      ResponseEntity.ok("""
+        <html>
+          <body>
+            <h1>Payment Processing</h1>
+            <p>Your payment is being processed. You'll receive a confirmation email shortly.</p>
+          </body>
+        </html>
+      """.trimIndent())
+    }
+  }
+  
+  @GetMapping("/payment/{orderId}/cancel")
+  suspend fun paymentCancel(
+    @PathVariable orderId: String
+  ): ResponseEntity<String> {
+    return ResponseEntity.ok("""
+      <html>
+        <body>
+          <h1>Payment Cancelled</h1>
+          <p>Your payment was cancelled. You can try again.</p>
+        </body>
+      </html>
+    """.trimIndent())
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Stripe Dashboard Setup
+
+### 1. Create Product and Price
+
+```bash
+# Using Stripe CLI
+stripe products create \
+  --name "Premium Plan" \
+  --description "Access to premium features"
+
+# Output: prod_XXXXXXXXXX
+
+stripe prices create \
+  --product prod_XXXXXXXXXX \
+  --unit-amount 2999 \
+  --currency usd
+
+# Output: price_XXXXXXXXXX
+```
+
+### 2. Configure Webhook
+
+1. Go to https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
+2. Click "Add endpoint"
+3. Enter webhook URL: `https://yourapp.com/api/stripe/webhook`
+4. Select events:
+   - `checkout.session.completed`
+   - `checkout.session.expired`
+   - `payment_intent.succeeded`
+   - `payment_intent.payment_failed`
+   - `payment_intent.canceled`
+5. Copy the webhook secret (starts with `whsec_`)
+6. Add to your environment: `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_XXX`
+
+## Frontend Integration
+
+### React Example
+
+```typescript
+// Checkout button component
+import { useState } from 'react';
+
+export function CheckoutButton({ productId }: { productId: string }) {
+  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
+  
+  const handleCheckout = async () => {
+    setLoading(true);
+    
+    try {
+      // Call your backend to create payment session
+      const response = await fetch('/api/checkout/create', {
+        method: 'POST',
+        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
+        body: JSON.stringify({ productId })
+      });
+      
+      const { checkoutUrl } = await response.json();
+      
+      // Redirect to Stripe Checkout
+      window.location.href = checkoutUrl;
+    } catch (error) {
+      console.error('Checkout failed:', error);
+      setLoading(false);
+    }
+  };
+  
+  return (
+    <button 
+      onClick={handleCheckout}
+      disabled={loading}
+    >
+      {loading ? 'Processing...' : 'Buy Now'}
+    </button>
+  );
+}
+```
+
+## Environment Variables
+
+Create a `.env` file or set environment variables:
+
+```bash
+# Development (Test Mode)
+export STRIPE_API_KEY=sk_test_51XXXXX
+export STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_XXXXX
+
+# Production (Live Mode)
+export STRIPE_API_KEY=sk_live_51XXXXX
+export STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_XXXXX
+```
+
+## Testing Locally
+
+### 1. Install Stripe CLI
+
+```bash
+brew install stripe/stripe-cli/stripe
+```
+
+### 2. Login to Stripe
+
+```bash
+stripe login
+```
+
+### 3. Forward Webhooks to Local Server
+
+```bash
+# Terminal 1: Start your app
+./gradlew bootRun
+
+# Terminal 2: Forward webhooks
+stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8080/api/stripe/webhook
+```
+
+The CLI will output a webhook secret like: `whsec_XXXXX`
+
+### 4. Test Payment Flow
+
+```bash
+# Trigger a test event
+stripe trigger checkout.session.completed
+```
+
+### 5. Test Cards
+
+Use these test card numbers in Stripe Checkout:
+- **Success**: 4242 4242 4242 4242
+- **Decline**: 4000 0000 0000 0002
+- **3D Secure**: 4000 0025 0000 3155
+- Any future expiry date (e.g., 12/34)
+- Any 3-digit CVC
+
+## Common Issues
+
+### Issue: Webhook signature verification fails
+
+**Solution**: Make sure you're using the correct webhook secret. For local development with Stripe CLI, use the secret provided by `stripe listen` command, not the one from the dashboard.
+
+### Issue: Payment succeeds but order not updated
+
+**Solution**: Check that:
+1. Webhook endpoint is publicly accessible
+2. Webhook secret is correct
+3. Order ID is included in session metadata
+4. Check application logs for errors
+
+### Issue: Unable to create payment session
+
+**Solution**: Verify:
+1. API key is valid and has correct permissions
+2. Product ID and Price ID exist in Stripe
+3. Price is active and available
+
+## Monitoring
+
+View payment events in:
+- **Stripe Dashboard**: https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments
+- **Webhook Logs**: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
+- **Application Logs**: Check your application logs for payment processing
+
+## Security Best Practices
+
+1. ✅ Always verify webhooks using signature
+2. ✅ Never expose API keys in client-side code
+3. ✅ Use environment variables for configuration
+4. ✅ Validate order ownership before creating payment
+5. ✅ Always rely on webhook for payment confirmation, not return URL
+6. ✅ Use test mode for development
+7. ✅ Implement idempotency for webhook handlers
+
