+# Stripe Payments Module
+
+This module provides integration with Stripe for handling payment transactions.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Payment Sessions**: Create Stripe Checkout sessions for products managed in Stripe
+- **Webhook Handling**: Process Stripe webhook events with signature verification
+- **Payment Tracking**: Query payment status and transaction history
+- **Coroutine Support**: Full Kotlin coroutines support for async operations
+
+## Configuration
+
+Add the following properties to your `application.yml` or `application.properties`:
+
+```yaml
+stripe:
+  api-key: ${STRIPE_API_KEY:sk_test_your_key_here}
+  webhook-secret: ${STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET:whsec_your_secret_here}
+```
+
+Or in `application.properties`:
+
+```properties
+stripe.api-key=${STRIPE_API_KEY:sk_test_your_key_here}
+stripe.webhook-secret=${STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET:whsec_your_secret_here}
+```
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+- `STRIPE_API_KEY`: Your Stripe secret API key (starts with `sk_test_` or `sk_live_`)
+- `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`: Your Stripe webhook signing secret (starts with `whsec_`)
+
+## Usage
+
+### Creating a Payment Session
+
+```kotlin
+@Autowired
+lateinit var paymentService: PaymentService
+
+suspend fun createPayment() {
+    val session = paymentService.createPaymentSession(
+        productId = "prod_XXXXXXXXXX",  // Stripe Product ID
+        priceId = "price_XXXXXXXXXX",    // Stripe Price ID
+        userId = userId,
+        orderId = orderId,
+        successUrl = "https://yourapp.com/payment/success",
+        cancelUrl = "https://yourapp.com/payment/cancel",
+        metadata = mapOf("customKey" to "customValue")
+    )
+    
+    // Redirect user to session.checkoutUrl
+}
+```
+
+### Handling Webhooks
+
+The webhook controller is automatically configured at `/api/stripe/webhook`.
+
+Configure this URL in your Stripe Dashboard:
+1. Go to https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
+2. Click "Add endpoint"
+3. Enter your webhook URL: `https://yourapp.com/api/stripe/webhook`
+4. Select events to listen for:
+   - `checkout.session.completed`
+   - `payment_intent.succeeded`
+   - `payment_intent.payment_failed`
+   - `checkout.session.expired`
+   - `payment_intent.canceled`
+
+### Retrieving Payment Status
+
+```kotlin
+// Get session status
+val session = paymentService.getPaymentSession(sessionId)
+
+// Get all payments for an order
+val payments = paymentService.getPaymentsByOrderId(orderId)
+```
+
+## Product Management
+
+Products and prices are managed directly in Stripe Dashboard:
+
+1. **Create Product**: Go to https://dashboard.stripe.com/products
+2. **Add Pricing**: Configure one-time or recurring pricing
+3. **Copy IDs**: Use the Product ID (`prod_XXX`) and Price ID (`price_XXX`) in your code
+
+## Testing
+
+### Test Mode
+
+Use test API keys (starting with `sk_test_`) for development:
+
+```bash
+export STRIPE_API_KEY=sk_test_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
+export STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
+```
+
+### Test Cards
+
+Use Stripe's test card numbers:
+- Success: `4242 4242 4242 4242`
+- Decline: `4000 0000 0000 0002`
+- Authentication: `4000 0025 0000 3155`
+
+See more: https://stripe.com/docs/testing
+
+### Webhook Testing
+
+Use Stripe CLI to forward webhooks to your local environment:
+
+```bash
+# Install Stripe CLI
+brew install stripe/stripe-cli/stripe
+
+# Login
+stripe login
+
+# Forward webhooks
+stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8080/api/stripe/webhook
+
+# Copy the webhook secret (whsec_XXX) to your configuration
+```
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────┐
+│  PaymentService     │  (Interface in domain module)
+│  (Interface)        │
+└──────────┬──────────┘
+           │ implements
+           │
+┌──────────▼──────────┐
+│  StripeService      │  (Implementation in stripe-payments module)
+│  @Service           │
+└──────────┬──────────┘
+           │
+           │ used by
+           │
+┌──────────▼───────────────┐
+│  StripeWebhookController │  (server-core module)
+│  /api/stripe/webhook     │
+└──────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+## Security
+
+- **Webhook Signature Verification**: All webhooks are verified using Stripe's signature
+- **API Key Security**: Never commit API keys to version control
+- **Use Environment Variables**: Configure keys via environment variables
+- **Production Keys**: Use live keys (`sk_live_`) only in production
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- `com.stripe:stripe-java:29.1.0` - Official Stripe Java SDK
+- Kotlin Coroutines for async operations
+- Spring Boot for dependency injection
+
+## Error Handling
+
+The service throws `PaymentServiceException` for payment-related errors:
+
+```kotlin
+try {
+    val session = paymentService.createPaymentSession(...)
+} catch (e: PaymentServiceException) {
+    log.error("Payment failed: ${e.message}", e)
+    // Handle error
+}
+```
+
+## Logging
+
+The service logs all important events:
+- Payment session creation
+- Webhook event processing
+- Payment status changes
+- Errors and exceptions
+
+Set logging level in your configuration:
+
+```yaml
+logging:
+  level:
+    org.migor.feedless.payment.stripe: DEBUG
+```
+
